h of Baron's $1B SpaceX IPO order flows into Baron Partners Fund (BPTIX)?","baron_partners_share_of_public_funds_pct":64.5,"baron_partners_share_of_firm_wide_pct":26.1,"bp_nav_usd":18700000000,"primary_dilution_pct":4.24,"anti_dilution_firmwide_usd":632639831,"anti_dilution_baron_partners_usd":164843220,"scenarios":[{"label":"Pro-rata across ALL Baron SpaceX vehicles (incl. private BaronX)","basis_pct":26.1,"full_fill":{"to_baron_partners_usd":260564088,"pct_of_bp_nav":1.39},"half_fill":{"to_baron_partners_usd":130282044,"pct_of_bp_nav":0.7}},{"label":"Pro-rata across PUBLIC open-end mutual funds only","basis_pct":64.5,"full_fill":{"to_baron_partners_usd":645400000,"pct_of_bp_nav":3.45},"half_fill":{"to_baron_partners_usd":322700000,"pct_of_bp_nav":1.73}}],"share_class_note":"IPO shares accrue to the FUND and are shared across its 3 classes (BPTRX retail, BPTIX institutional, BPTUX R6) pro-rata by NAV — so BPTIX automatically gets its AUM-proportional slice. Retail BPTRX was ~$4.16B (MSN); BPTIX/BPTUX make up the rest of the ~$18.7B fund.","bottom_line":"No public source discloses the per-fund split (NOT FOUND). Baron Partners holds ~65% of Baron's PUBLIC-fund SpaceX but ~26% of firm-wide SpaceX (the private BaronX vehicles hold ~$5.5B at ~99%). So a fully-filled $1B order plausibly sends ~$260M-$650M into Baron Partners Fund = ~1.4%-3.5% of its $18.7B NAV in incremental SpaceX, on top of the existing ~27%. Incremental, not transformational — and the fill itself is uncertain. The order is bought at the $135 IPO price, which the fund already marks SpaceX at (since 6/4), so it adds exposure/shares without an immediate markup.","confidence":"Bases are MEASURED (SEC+Baron letter); the split itself is UNDISCLOSED inference."}}